Origin: mammoth-lts, fix of the backports of GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 / GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7 (patches 9018 / 9019) to PHP < 8.1
Imported-by: mammoth-lts 7.2 backport (patches/7.2/9023-mysqlnd-do-not-free-malformed-row-fields-twice.patch), applies as-is to 7.1

From a8cd385c26c294b6363179b71513a1bbb0c666f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu GILLOOTS <mathieu@itmg-consulting.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:04:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mysqlnd: do not free the fields of a malformed row twice

The fixes for GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 and GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7 (written for PHP 8.1+) free the fields already decoded
when a row packet turns out to be malformed. Before PHP 8.1, buffered results keep the decoded rows in set->data,
and free_result() frees every field again: heap use-after-free / double free that a malicious MySQL server (or a
man-in-the-middle on a plaintext connection) can trigger. Found by AddressSanitizer with the advisories' own tests.

Leave the freed fields undecoded (IS_UNDEF), which free_result() skips. PHP 8.1+ is not affected (the decoded rows
are no longer cached there).
---
 ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c b/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c
index c67d3f61..b3458589 100644
--- a/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c
+++ b/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_wireprotocol.c
@@ -1678,6 +1678,8 @@ php_mysqlnd_rowp_read_binary_protocol(MYSQLND_MEMORY_POOL_CHUNK * row_buffer, zv
 			if (rbs <= row_position) {
 				for (j = 0, current_field = start_field; j < i; current_field++, j++) {
 					zval_ptr_dtor(current_field);
+					/* buffered results keep the decoded row: leave it undecoded, or free_result() frees these fields again */
+					ZVAL_UNDEF(current_field);
 				}
 				php_error_docref(NULL, E_WARNING, "Malformed server packet. No packet space left for the field");
 				DBG_RETURN(FAIL);
@@ -1686,6 +1688,8 @@ php_mysqlnd_rowp_read_binary_protocol(MYSQLND_MEMORY_POOL_CHUNK * row_buffer, zv
 			if (p == NULL) {
 				for (j = 0, current_field = start_field; j < i; current_field++, j++) {
 					zval_ptr_dtor(current_field);
+					/* buffered results keep the decoded row: leave it undecoded, or free_result() frees these fields again */
+					ZVAL_UNDEF(current_field);
 				}
 				DBG_RETURN(FAIL);
 			}
@@ -1770,6 +1774,8 @@ php_mysqlnd_rowp_read_text_protocol_aux(MYSQLND_MEMORY_POOL_CHUNK * row_buffer,
 			php_error_docref(NULL, E_WARNING, "Malformed server packet. Field length pointing after end of packet");
 			for (j = 0, current_field = start_field; j < i; current_field++, j++) {
 				zval_ptr_dtor(current_field);
+				/* buffered results keep the decoded row: leave it undecoded, or free_result() frees these fields again */
+				ZVAL_UNDEF(current_field);
 			}
 			DBG_RETURN(FAIL);
 		} else {
